## Use time = distance ÷ speed
\text{Time} &= \frac{120}{180}
&= \frac{2}{3}
ANSWER: \frac{2}{3} \text{ hour}

## Time from A to B
T_1 &= \frac{2}{3}
## Time from B to A
T_2 &= \frac{120}{220}
&= \frac{6}{11}
## Add the times and find the total distance
Total distance there and back is $2 \times 120 = 240$ km.
\text{Total time} &= \frac{2}{3} + \frac{6}{11}
&= \frac{22}{33} + \frac{18}{33}
&= \frac{40}{33}
## Average speed = total distance ÷ total time
\text{Average speed} &= \frac{240}{\frac{40}{33}}
&= 240 \times \frac{33}{40}
&= 198
ANSWER: 198 \text{ km/hour}

## Identify a, b and c
Compare $9x^2 + 6x - 5 = 0$ with $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$.
a &= 9
b &= 6
c &= -5
## Write the quadratic formula
x &= \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
## Substitute a, b and c
x &= \frac{-6 \pm \sqrt{6^2 - 4(9)(-5)}}{2(9)}
x &= \frac{-6 \pm \sqrt{36 + 180}}{18}
x &= \frac{-6 \pm \sqrt{216}}{18}
## Find the root using the plus sign
x &= \frac{-6 + \sqrt{216}}{18}
x &= \frac{-6 + 14.697}{18}
x &\approx 0.483
x &\approx 0.48
## Find the root using the minus sign
x &= \frac{-6 - \sqrt{216}}{18}
x &= \frac{-6 - 14.697}{18}
x &\approx -1.150
x &\approx -1.15
ANSWER: x \approx 0.48 \text{ or } x \approx -1.15

## Substitute S = 15 into the formula
C &= \frac{1000}{15 + 10}
C &= \frac{1000}{25}
C &= 40
ANSWER: C = 40

## Multiply both sides by S + 10
C &= \frac{1000}{S + 10}
C(S + 10) &= 1000
## Expand the bracket
CS + 10C &= 1000
## Subtract 10C from both sides
CS &= 1000 - 10C
## Divide both sides by C
S &= \frac{1000 - 10C}{C}
ANSWER: S = \frac{1000 - 10C}{C}

## Find S when C = 30
$C$ gets smaller as $S$ gets bigger, so $C = 30$ gives the largest $S$.
S &= \frac{1000 - 10(30)}{30}
S &= \frac{1000 - 300}{30}
S &= \frac{700}{30}
S &\approx 23.33
## Find S when C = 100
S &= \frac{1000 - 10(100)}{100}
S &= \frac{1000 - 1000}{100}
S &= 0
## State the range
$S$ goes from $0$ to about $23.3$.
ANSWER: S \text{ goes from } 0 \text{ to } 23.3

