## Write the slope formula
Slope $m = \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$ for points $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$.
## Substitute A(4, 2) and B(1, 8)
m &= \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}
&= \frac{8 - 2}{1 - 4}
&= \frac{6}{-3}
&= -2
ANSWER: m = -2

## Write the distance formula
$|AB| = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$
## Substitute A(4, 2) and B(1, 8)
|AB| &= \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
&= \sqrt{(1 - 4)^2 + (8 - 2)^2}
&= \sqrt{(-3)^2 + 6^2}
&= \sqrt{9 + 36}
&= \sqrt{45}
## Simplify the surd
\sqrt{45} &= \sqrt{9 \times 5}
&= 3\sqrt{5}
ANSWER: |AB| = \sqrt{45} = 3\sqrt{5}

